error[DZ0502]: `300` does not fit in `u8`
  ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:5:18
  │
5 │     World      = 300
  │                  ^^^ outside the range of `u8`
  │
  = help: valid values are 0 to 255

error[DZ0517]: a struct field cannot hold `&Vec3`
   ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:23:17
   │
23 │     borrowed:   &Vec3
   │                 ^^^^^ references live only on the stack
   │
   = help: use `^T` for a stored pointer — a reference in a field could outlive what it points at, and Dazzle has no lifetimes to catch that (spec §5.2)

error[DZ0507]: cannot assign to `count`
   ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:34:9
   │
34 │         count += 1
   │         ^^^^^ not mutable
   │
   = help: declare it as `let mut count` to allow assignment

error[DZ0501]: expected `i64`, found `i32`
   ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:39:12
   │
39 │     return small
   │            ^^^^^ this is `i32`
   │
   = help: Dazzle has no implicit numeric conversions, not even widening (spec §5.1) — write `... as i64`

error[DZ0502]: `300` does not fit in `u8`
   ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:43:17
   │
43 │     let b: u8 = 300
   │                 ^^^ outside the range of `u8`
   │
   = help: valid values are 0 to 255

error[DZ0514]: `+` cannot mix `i32` and `i64`
   ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:47:12
   │
47 │     return a + b
   │            ^^^^^ operands have different types
   │
   = help: Dazzle has no implicit numeric conversions, not even widening (spec §5.1) — cast one side with `as`

error[DZ0508]: `if` needs a `bool`, found `i32`
   ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:51:8
   │
51 │     if n {
   │        ^ this is `i32`
   │
   = help: there is no truthiness in Dazzle — compare explicitly, e.g. `x != 0` or `p != null` (spec §10.1)

error[DZ0508]: `while` needs a `bool`, found `Vec3`
   ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:57:11
   │
57 │     while v {
   │           ^ this is `Vec3`
   │
   = help: there is no truthiness in Dazzle — compare explicitly, e.g. `x != 0` or `p != null` (spec §10.1)

error[DZ0505]: `Vec3` has no field `w`
   ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:63:14
   │
63 │     return v.w
   │              ^ unknown field
   │
   = help: did you mean `x`?

error[DZ0506]: field `Counter::count` is not visible here
   ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:67:14
   │
21 │     count:      u32
   │     ----- declared here
   ·
67 │     return c.count
   │              ^^^^^ private field
   │
   = help: this field is private to `Counter`; mark it `pub` or `pub(module)` (spec §4)

error[DZ0520]: `Counter` has no method `increment`
   ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:71:14
   │
71 │     return c.increment()
