error[DZ0511]: cannot cast `Vec3` to `i32`
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:100:12
    │
100 │     return v as i32
    │            ^^^^^^^^ invalid conversion
    │
    = help: `as` converts between numbers, between pointers, and from an enum to its backing type; it never runs user code (spec §10.6)

error[DZ0515]: `i32` cannot be indexed
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:104:12
    │
104 │     return n[0]
    │            ^ not an array or slice

error[DZ0518]: `i32` cannot be dereferenced
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:108:12
    │
108 │     return n^
    │            ^^ not a pointer
    │
    = help: postfix `^` dereferences a `^T`; `.` already reaches through pointers on its own (spec §5.2)

error[DZ0513]: `switch` on `Shape` is not exhaustive
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:112:5
    │  
112 │ ╭     switch s {
113 │ │         case Circle(c) {
114 │ │             return 1
115 │ │         }
    · │
118 │ │         }
119 │ │     }
    │ ╰─────^ `Point` not covered
    │  
    = help: add the missing arms, or a `default` arm (spec §10.3)

error[DZ0505]: `Shape` has no variant `Triangle`
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:125:14
    │
125 │         case Triangle {
    │              ^^^^^^^^ unknown variant

error[DZ0510]: fallible call not consumed
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:151:5
    │
151 │     may_fail()
    │     ^^^^^^^^^^ this may fail, and the failure is discarded
    │
    = help: add an `or` clause: `or return` to propagate, `or <value>` to fall back, or `or ignore` to drop it deliberately (spec §9.7)

error[DZ0516]: the failure has nowhere to go
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:156:27
    │
156 │     let v = may_fail() or return
    │                           ^^^^^^ `or return` propagates, and this signature cannot carry it
    │
    = help: mark this function `!->`, or handle the failure here with a                          fallback or a block (spec §9.5)

error[DZ0525]: `or` needs something that can fail, found `i32`
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:162:12
    │
162 │     return n or 0
    │            ^ this cannot fail
    │
    = help: `or` applies to a fallible call, a `T?`, or a `^T` (spec §9.4)

error[DZ0523]: `i32?` has no failure value to bind as `e`
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:167:26
    │
167 │     let v = maybe() or { e ->
    │                          ^ nothing to bind here
    │
    = help: only a fallible call carries an `Error`; write `or { … }` with no binding (spec §9.4)

error[DZ0523]: this `or` clause produces `str`, but `i32` is needed
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:175:24
    │
175 │     let v = maybe() or "not an i32"
    │                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is `str`
    │
    = help: an `or` clause must produce the success type or diverge (spec §9.4)

error[DZ0501]: cannot bind a value of type `void`
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:181:13
    │
181 │     let v = may_fail() or ignore
    │             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this expression produces no value

error[DZ0524]: `ignore` produces no value
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:181:27
    │
181 │     let v = may_fail() or ignore
    │                           ^^^^^^ nothing to bind here
    │
    = help: `or ignore` is statement position only; to keep a value supply a fallback instead (spec §9.4)

error[DZ0522]: expected `&i32`, found `^i32`
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:187:15
    │
187 │     takes_ref(a_pointer())
    │               ^^^^^^^^^^^ a pointer may be null; a reference may not
    │
    = help: check it once where it enters scope: `let x = p or return`, or `or unreachable` if it provably cannot be null (spec §5.2)

error[DZ0521]: `none` needs an optional type here
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:191:13
    │
191 │     let x = none
    │             ^^^^ nothing here expects a `T?`
    │
    = help: `none` is the empty case of `T?` (spec §9.1)

error[DZ0501]: `i32` cannot be iterated
    ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:196:14
    │
196 │     for i in n {
    │              ^ not iterable
    │
    = help: `for` works over ranges, arrays and slices; user types need the `Iterate` trait, which arrives with generics (spec §8.5)

